      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `JsonIncludeProperties.Value.from()` throws a `NullPointerException` when the annotation's `order()` method returns `null` (because `null.asBoolean()` is called on the result). I'll improve understandability by giving meaningful names and removing cryptic auto-generated comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: renamed the auto-generated variable `jsonIncludeProperties0` to `mockAnnotation` for clarity, removed the cryptic `// Undeclared exception!` and empty catch-block comments, and added a Javadoc explaining exactly why the `NullPointerException` is expected — all without altering the runtime behaviour."
